---
import PlatformIcon from './PlatformIcon.astro';
const webUrl = 'https://d2cpue9r0hnyl3.cloudfront.net/';
---

<section aria-labelledby="install-title" class="install-options">
  <h2 id="install-title">Install</h2>
  <div class="install-web" id="web-install">
    <h3><PlatformIcon platform="web" size={24} />Web / PWA</h3>
    <p><a href={webUrl}>Open the web edition</a> in your browser on a phone, tablet or computer. You can also install it as an app; it works offline after the first load.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Android:</strong> open the web edition in Chrome, then choose <strong>⋮ → Install and create shortcut → Install</strong> (or <strong>Add to Home screen</strong> on older versions) and follow the prompt.</li>
      <li><strong>iPhone / iPad:</strong> open it in Safari, choose <strong>Share → Add to Home Screen</strong>, enable <strong>Open as Web App</strong> if shown, then tap <strong>Add</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Computer:</strong> in Chrome or Edge, use the install button in the address bar when offered.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The web edition is the original hypertext journey. The Android APKs below are the native 3D adventure.</p>
  </div>

  <details class="install-guide" id="android-install">
    <summary><span class="install-icons"><PlatformIcon platform="phone" size={24} /><PlatformIcon platform="tablet" size={24} /></span><span>Android phone / tablet</span></summary>
    <div class="install-body">
      <p><strong>Before you start:</strong> the current APK requires Android 8.0 or later and an ARM device (32-bit or 64-bit). The same APK is packaged for Android phones, tablets and Google TV. Use the newest build below unless you want to revisit an older milestone.</p>

      <h3>Download and install on the same device</h3>
      <p>You only need the phone or tablet you want to install on, a browser and an internet connection to download the APK. Developer options and USB debugging are not required.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open this page in the browser on the phone or tablet you want to use and tap the newest <a href="#native-milestones-title">APK download below</a>.</li>
        <li>Open the downloaded <code>.apk</code> from your browser’s downloads or the Files app.</li>
        <li>If Android blocks installation, tap <strong>Settings</strong> in the prompt and enable <strong>Allow from this source</strong> for the app opening the APK. You can also find this under <strong>Settings → Apps → Special app access → Install unknown apps</strong>; names vary by device. On Android 5–7, look for <strong>Settings → Security → Unknown sources</strong> instead.</li>
        <li>Return to the APK, tap <strong>Install</strong>, then <strong>Open</strong>. The app appears as <strong>Finding Your Way</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>You can turn off <strong>Allow from this source</strong> again after installation. See <a href="https://support.google.com/pixelphone/answer/7391672?hl=en">Google’s APK installation instructions</a>.</p>

    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="install-guide" id="chromecast-install">
    <summary><span class="install-icons"><PlatformIcon platform="tv" size={24} /></span><span>Chromecast with Google TV</span></summary>
    <div class="install-body">
      <p><strong>Before you start:</strong> use a Chromecast with Google TV or another Android TV / Google TV device that can install apps, an Android phone, and the TV remote. Connect the phone and TV to the same Wi-Fi network. The older, cast-only Chromecast cannot install an APK.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Install <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.yablio.sendfilestotv">Send files to TV</a> from Google Play on both your phone and TV. On the TV, also install a file manager that can open APK files if you do not already have one.</li>
        <li>Open this page on your phone and tap the newest <a href="#native-milestones-title">APK download below</a>. Keep the downloaded APK on the phone; you do not need to install it there.</li>
        <li>On the TV, open <strong>Send files to TV</strong> and select <strong>Receive</strong>. On the phone, open the same app, select <strong>Send</strong>, choose the APK in <strong>Downloads</strong>, and select your TV. Allow the transfer app’s requested file-access permissions.</li>
        <li>On the TV, open the received APK. If the transfer app cannot open it, use the TV file manager to open it from <strong>Download</strong> or the receiving folder you selected.</li>
        <li>If installation is blocked, allow the app opening the APK to <strong>Install unknown apps</strong>. Look under <strong>Settings → Apps → Security &amp; restrictions → Unknown sources</strong> or <strong>Special app access → Install unknown apps</strong>; names vary by TV.</li>
        <li>If that permission is unavailable, use the TV remote to open <strong>Settings → System → About</strong> and select <strong>Android TV OS build</strong> seven times until developer mode is enabled. On other Android TVs, look for <strong>About → Build</strong>. Return to the unknown-app setting, allow the installer app, and reopen the APK.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>Install</strong>, then launch <strong>Finding Your Way</strong> from the TV’s apps. Use the TV remote or a connected gamepad to play.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>This method needs no computer, USB debugging or wireless debugging. Developer options are not needed on the phone. You can revoke the TV installer app’s unknown-app permission after installation.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

</section>

<style>
  .install-web, .install-guide { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); }
  .install-web { padding-bottom: 12px; }
  .install-web h3 { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
  .install-guide > summary {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 14px 0; cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 15px;
  }
  .install-guide > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .install-guide > summary::after { content: '▸'; color: var(--color-primary-container); }
  .install-guide[open] > summary::after { content: '▾'; }
  .install-guide > summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary-container); outline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .install-icons { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; }
  .install-body { padding: 0 0 12px; min-width: 0; }
  .install-body h3 { margin-top: 20px; }
  .install-options li + li { margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
